    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d25">

                <pb facs="0071" n="17" xml:id="pg17"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">President Roosevelt to Prime Minister
                        Churchill</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d25-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">priority</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName>U.S.S. “<hi
                                rendition="#small-caps">Cummings</hi>”</placeName>,<anchor n="2"
                            xml:id="d25-f2"/>] <date calendar="gregorian" when="1944-08-11">11
                            August 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Number 597 personal and top secret from the President for the Former Naval
                    Person.</p>
                <p>Your 750<anchor n="3" xml:id="d25-f3"/> is received at sea. I also deeply regret
                    my inability to come to Scotland for this meeting.</p>
                <p>It appears now that I should be able to arrive in Quebec on the 10th or 11th of
                    September for a meeting of the Combined Staff on the Teheran scale.</p>
                <p>My consultations with the military and naval commanders in the Pacific area have
                    been most interesting and valuable.<anchor n="4" xml:id="d25-f4"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Roosevelt</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d25-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d25-f1-content">
                <p>Sent to the White House Map Room as telegram No. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >Blue</hi> 106; forwarded to the United States Naval Attaché, London, via
                    Navy channels.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d25-f2" n="2" xml:id="d25-f2-content">
                <p>Roosevelt was en route from Auk Bay, Alaska, to Bremerton, Washington. See <hi
                        rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg10">p. 10</ref>, fn. 1.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d25-f3" n="3" xml:id="d25-f3-content">
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg15">p. 15</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d25-f4" n="4" xml:id="d25-f4-content">
                <p>Concerning Roosevelt’s conferences with MacArthur and Nimitz, July 27–28, 1944,
                    see Matloff, p. 482; Leahy, pp. 250–251.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
